# HIMS runs only in Docker. Every setting is documented in .env.docker.example:
#
#   cp .env.docker.example .env.docker
#
# There is no cloud configuration (no hosted database, Redis or file store) and
# no .env.local. Host-side scripts (npm run db:*, npm test) read DATABASE_URL
# and the other variables only from the environment you set explicitly, never
# from a file, so they cannot target a database by accident.
